{
  "key": "ifrs-generic",
  "version": 8,
  "name_ar": "دليل حسابات عام وفق المعايير الدولية",
  "name_en": "Generic IFRS chart of accounts",
  "countries": [],
  "source": {
    "title": "IFRS presentation requirements - IAS 1 Presentation of Financial Statements, with IAS 21 and IFRS 9 for the classifications",
    "url": "https://www.ifrs.org/issued-standards/list-of-standards/",
    "note": "IFRS does not prescribe a chart of accounts and no standard contains one. IAS 1 prescribes what the statements must present; this chart is a minimal structure that can produce those statements, and nothing more. The two classifications that are NOT presentation choices are marked per account: `monetary` is the IAS 21 distinction that decides what is restated at the closing rate, and the expected credit loss provision follows IFRS 9. Used for any entity whose country has no template of its own - deliberately generic rather than the nearest-looking national chart, because a chart that is almost right is harder to correct than one that is plainly a starting point."
  },
